scription":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1609442062,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjA5NDQyMDYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:shaders","name":"topic:shaders","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-05-28T02:57:50Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T18:58:44Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.6\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10700K CPU @ 3.80GHz (16 threads) - 63.74 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nUniforms have issues knowing what is constant and what isn't:\n```\n//none of this errors\nconst float CONSTANT_EXPRESSION = 2.0*2.0;\nconst float ONE = 1.0;\nconst float MULTIPLY_CONSTANTS = ONE * CONSTANT_EXPRESSION;\n//while these do with this error: Expected constant expression after '='\nuniform float error_simple_expression = ONE;\nuniform float error_expression = 2.0 * 2.0;\nuniform float error_expression_two = MULTIPLY_CONSTANTS;\nuniform float error_expression_three = ONE * ONE;\n```\n\nThis makes it impossible to use things like PI in uniform expressions, this also extends to instance uniform variables\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\njust type given code into shader editor and the debugger will error.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119836/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,